# Patterns here match against the whole build context, but a bare name like
# `node_modules` only ever matches at the TOP level — it does not match
# `web/node_modules`. That distinction matters here: the storefront stage runs
# `COPY web/ ./` after its own `npm ci`, so an unignored `web/node_modules` from
# a developer's working copy is copied straight over the freshly installed one.
# When the two platforms differ — a Windows or macOS checkout building a Linux
# image — the Vite build then dies on a missing esbuild or rollup binary,
# because npm installs those as platform-specific optional dependencies.
#
# The `**/` prefixes are therefore load-bearing, not redundant.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.log

# Every environment file, at any depth.
#
# No stage copies one today, but this is defence in depth: the day someone adds
# a `COPY . .`, production credentials would be baked into an image layer and
# travel with it into the registry. Far cheaper to prevent than to discover.
**/.env
**/.env.*

.git
.gitignore
.github
docker-compose.yml
README.md

# Internal notes, and the platform's local scratch directories.
docs
.railway
.railway-config-pull-*

# Safaricom's initiator certificates and any other key material. These belong in
# the platform's secret store and are mounted at runtime, never baked into an
# image.
certs
service_account.json
